.TH DANBY-VIOLETSANTSRODENTS 1
.SH NAME
danby-violetsantsrodents \- mutualism and predation in a three-species network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/violetsantsrodents
.SH MODEL
Violets grow logistically.  Ant activity adds a saturating seed-dispersal
benefit.  Rodents consume violets, while ants reduce effective rodent grazing.
Ants reproduce from violet service and both animal populations have independent
mortality.  Thus the model contains mutualism, consumption, and indirect
protection rather than a simple linear food chain.
.SH DISPLAY
Separate histories and editable current-state bars preserve all three species.
The eight tracks control violet growth and capacity, ant benefit, rodent
grazing, ant conversion and death, ant deterrence, and rodent death.
